title: The Words of God – Jack Hyles on Inspiration
description: A lesson from Jack Hyles on the inspiration of Scripture: God the Penman, men the pens, and the words of God preserved in the King James Bible.
output: lessons/others/hyles-on-inspiration.html

# Converted from the hand-made page lessons/others/hyles-on-inspiration.html (4 slides, same order).
# The Hyles quotations are set to the sermon text "How We Got God's Word", from his book The Need for an Every-Word Bible
# (as printed at jesus-is-savior.com). Where the old page differed from that text, the printed text is used.

=== I. God, the Penman
--- The Words of God [title]
overline: A Lesson from Jack Hyles on the Inspiration of Scripture
heading: The Words of God
sub: Pens in the Hand of the Penman
quote: The words of God were given to us by God and not by holy men. They were given to us by God through holy men, using them to get the words to us. | Jack Hyles, “How We Got God’s Word”
quote: Sometimes that pen didn’t understand all he wrote. References in the Bible reveal how that some of these men did not know exactly what they were writing. | Jack Hyles, “How We Got God’s Word”
quote: Why? They were just pens; the Penman was doing the writing! God’s voice gave His Word through them, not to them. | Jack Hyles, “How We Got God’s Word”

=== II. If We Have No Perfect Bible
--- What Difference Does It Make?
quote: “Brother Hyles, so what if a preacher boy goes down to a so-called Christian college where he sits in a liberal professor’s class who teaches, ‘We have no perfect Bible.’ What difference does it make?” | Jack Hyles, “How We Got God’s Word”
quote: It makes all the difference in the world! | Jack Hyles, “How We Got God’s Word”
quote: What he better do is stop and realize that if we have no perfect English Bible, we cannot live because… | Jack Hyles, “How We Got God’s Word”
scripture: Matthew 4:4 | mark: Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceedeth out of the mouth of God

=== III. A Preacher’s Conviction
--- I Would Walk Out of This Pulpit
quote: If I did not believe that every word in the Bible had been preserved from the time it was given through the mouth of men as God, the Penman, wrote with the pen of humanity, I would walk out of this pulpit, and I wouldn’t waste my life preaching. | Jack Hyles, “How We Got God’s Word”
quote: If there’s a word in the Bible that is wrong, no one knows which one it is, so it could be any of them. | Jack Hyles, “How We Got God’s Word”
quote: I believe that we have God’s preserved words for us in the King James Bible. | Jack Hyles, “How We Got God’s Word”
quote: In conclusion, how did we get God’s words? | Jack Hyles, “How We Got God’s Word”

=== IV. From Heaven to the King James Bible
--- How We Got God’s Words
point: | The words of God were always in Heaven.
point: | Man must have every word to live.
point: | God had to find a way to get every word to man.
point: | God chose men and made them holy, which means they were **“set apart or chosen”** to be God’s pens.
point: | God gave His words to us through those chosen men. God said, “I want you men to be My pens, and I will pick you up, and I will use you to write My words as the Penman. I will not use your brain; I will use your mouth.” God gave us the God-breathed Book. God’s breath across the vocal cords of human beings gave us His words.
point: | God has preserved His words for us in the **King James Bible.**
note: Jack Hyles, “How We Got God’s Word”
